obs The three folded-link drafts remain held for revision. Their scan classifies dead links by whether any tracked path shares the basename. It calls that class recoverable and ratchets the rest when FOLD_SHELF_LOST_MAX is set. The actual resolver also distinguishes ambiguity and supports sprigless timestamp recovery.
obs Extracted the parked control, scan, and its original repointer dependency into session-output/bakery-path-recovery. The complete control exits 0 with 93 yes readings and no no readings; all 86 control-output assertions in the parked witness find their expected literal. TMPDIR stays under this checkout and GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES prevents the non-repository pen from discovering the parent checkout. The initial run lacked the repointer and ceiling, so its partial output is not the completed control receipt.
obs Added two independent Git pens. With two tracked files sharing a basename, the draft reports links_stale=1, links_lost=0, verdict=ok at ceiling zero; the current resolver reports ambiguous and names both candidates. With a sprigless dated link and one renamed file carrying that stamp, the draft reports links_lost=1 and exits 1; the resolver reports recovered-by-stamp and names the file. Both are disagreements with the draft's stated recovery meaning. Neither counterexample changes tracked source.
obs Preserve the folded-link family until classification follows the resolver's actual verdicts and both counterexamples have controls. A matching basename alone proves neither a unique home nor the absence of other recovery paths. The draft also predates the current archive-depth handling; restoration needs integration with that newer behavior.
